Fix the rmtfs shared-memory node so it can actually bind.

sdm660.dtsi:1579 declares the rmtfs region with a ZERO base address:

    qcom,rmtfs_sharedmem@0 {
            compatible = "qcom,sharedmem-uio";
            reg = <0x0 0x200000>;
            reg-names = "rmtfs";
            qcom,client-id = <0x00000001>;
            qcom,guard-memory;
    };

drivers/uio/msm_sharedmem/msm_sharedmem.c:153 rejects that outright:

    if (shared_mem_pyhsical == 0) {
            pr_err("Shared memory base is zero\n");
            return -EINVAL;
    }

so the node never probes and /dev/uio* never appears.  rmtfs then has
nothing to serve the modem's RFSA file requests from, and the modem dies
right after the MBA hand-off.

Address chosen from the verified free gap in the reserved-memory map:

    0x85700000 +0x100000 -> 0x85800000   wlan_msa_mem
    0x85800000 +0x800000 -> 0x86000000   removed_regions
    0x86000000 +0x200000 -> 0x86200000   smem_mem
    0x86200000 +0x2d00000 -> 0x88f00000   removed_regions1
    <<< FREE: 0x88f00000 .. 0x8ac00000 = 29 MB >>>
    0x8ac00000 +0x7e00000 -> 0x92a00000   modem_fw_mem

0x88f00000 is 2 MB-aligned and 4 KB-aligned (guard-memory adds SZ_4K at
each end, msm_sharedmem.c:167).  It does not overlap any reserved region
and does not reach into modem_fw_mem.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/qcom/sdm660.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/qcom/sdm660.dtsi
@@ -1576,9 +1576,9 @@
 		};
 	};
 
-	qcom,rmtfs_sharedmem@0 {
+	qcom,rmtfs_sharedmem@88f00000 {
 		compatible = "qcom,sharedmem-uio";
-		reg = <0x0 0x200000>;
+		reg = <0x0 0x88f00000 0x0 0x200000>;
 		reg-names = "rmtfs";
 		qcom,client-id = <0x00000001>;
 		qcom,guard-memory;
